cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Trend Detective or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Trend Detective: real or random? Earth trends from NASA satellite data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jain
    given-names: Vinayak
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-10
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/entitySource/trend_detective"
url: "https://entitysource.github.io/trend_detective/"
abstract: >-
  An interactive web app for NASA Space Apps 2026 (Challenge 2, Be An Earth System Trend Detective). It tests 15
  satellite and measurement records (2003–2025) for real trends, with Mann-Kendall tests corrected for
  autocorrelation, Sen's slope and false-discovery-rate control across map cells, and checks its results against
  published science.
keywords:
  - climate
  - remote sensing
  - trend detection
  - Mann-Kendall
  - NASA Earthdata
  - education
